\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Cleaning Steps\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Step 1: Filter Status History File\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Open 
\f2\fs26 stathist_kipa.sas7bdat
\f1\fs24 . Filter to kidney and kidney-pancreas candidates:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 WL_ORG = "KI"  OR  WL_ORG = "KP"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Expected N = 2,167,709 rows
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Step 2: Deduplicate Candidate File\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Open 
\f2\fs26 cand_kipa.sas7bdat
\f1\fs24 . Check for duplicates by 
\f2\fs26 PX_ID
\f1\fs24 . One duplicate pair was identified (2 rows with the same 
\f2\fs26 PX_ID
\f1\fs24 ). The two rows were identical in all relevant variables; there was differences in 
\f2\fs26 CAN_TRR_EXISTS
\f1\fs24  (0 vs 1) and the duplicate case indicator. One row was retained.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Expected N = 1,213,405 unique rows after deduplication
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Step 3: Merge Status History and Candidate Files\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Merge the filtered status history file (Step 1) with the deduplicated candidate file (Step 2) to add candidate variables.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Linking variable:
\f1\b0  
\f2\fs26 PX_ID
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Step 4: Merge with Institution File\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Merge the file from Step 3 with 
\f2\fs26 institution.sas7bdat
\f1\fs24  to add transplant center variables, including the listing center's state.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Linking variables:
\f1\b0  
\f2\fs26 CAN_LISTING_CTR_CD
\f1\fs24  and 
\f2\fs26 CAN_LISTING_CTR_TY
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Step 5: Exclude Puerto Rico Listings\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Create variable based on the listing center's state from the institution file:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Puerto_Rico_Listing = 1  IF  PRIMARY_STATE = "PR"\
Puerto_Rico_Listing = 0  OTHERWISE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Filter to 
\f2\fs26 Puerto_Rico_Listing = 0
\f1\fs24 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 9,849 rows with Puerto Rico listings were excluded
\f1\b0  
\f0\b Expected N = 2,157,860 rows after exclusion
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Step 6: Save as CSV\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Save the filtered file as CSV for R processing. The R code for computing monthly active waitlist size (counting unique 
\f2\fs26 PERS_ID
\f1\fs24  with active status codes 4010, 4050, 4060, or 5010 in each month) and for the interrupted time series analysis is provided separately.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

